  <section id="gdr" class="briefing-slide tone-rose" aria-labelledby="gdr-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="gdr-title">{t('SD-LoRA 先训出来，GDR 再决定这次用不用', 'SD-LoRA is trained first; GDR then decides whether to use it')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('1.7B 这条线里，训练程序有 44 次都真的训练出了一个 SD-LoRA 候选。加入 GDR（Gated Delta Rule）以后，事情多了一步：候选先训出来，GDR 再看短期效果，决定这次参数到底要不要真的改到下一轮模型上。', 'In our original OpenEVO Stage 2 design, each parameter-evolution event trains an SD-LoRA update that enters the next model state. The 1.7B long-horizon run actually produced and trained 44 such updates. We later added GDR (Gated Delta Rule): train the update first, then use its short-term effect to decide whether it is written into the continuing model.')}</p>
      <div class="before-after gdr-flow">
        <div class="before"><span>{t('原本的参数进化', 'Original parameter evolution')}</span><strong>{t('满足训练条件 → 训练 SD-LoRA → 下一轮直接用', 'evolve → train SD-LoRA → update parameters')}</strong><p>{t('这一步已经进入实际 SD-LoRA 训练。1.7B 一共出现了 44 次这样的候选。', 'Each parameter-evolution event corresponds to one actually trained SD-LoRA candidate. The 1.7B line produced 44 of them.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>GDR = Gated Delta Rule</span><strong>{t('满足训练条件 → 训练 SD-LoRA → GDR 再说 yes / no', 'evolve → train SD-LoRA → gate it → decide whether to write')}</strong><p>{t('44 个候选都已经训练出来了，但 GDR 只同意 7 次真的改到下一轮模型上，另外 37 次被它拒绝。', 'All 44 updates were trained, but GDR admitted only 7 into later model states; the other 37 trained updates were rejected.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="bottom-claim">{t('所以 44 代表训练里真实发生的 44 次 SD-LoRA 候选。真正让我们警觉的是：已经训练了 44 次，最后只有 7 次真正影响后面的模型。于是问题变成：GDR 会不会筛得太保守？', 'So 44 counts the SD-LoRA parameter-evolution events that actually occurred in this run. Seeing 44 → 7 led to the next question: is GDR filtering too conservatively?')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('GDR 的判定逻辑与完整实验定义', 'GDR decision logic and full experimental definition')}</a></p>
