      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('我们有大量 checkpoint / round 记录，但“训练过程指标”和“冻结终评”从一开始就故意分开。这样 final panel 才不会在训练中被反复打开，变成调参集。', 'We have extensive checkpoint / round records, but training-process metrics and the frozen final evaluation were deliberately kept separate from the start. That keeps the final panel from being repeatedly opened during training and turned into a tuning set.')}</p>
      <div class="technical-grid">
        <article><span>01 · W&B</span><h3>{t('训练过程中已经有的曲线', 'Curves already recorded during training')}</h3><ul><li>{t('7B 记录：149 轮 Score + 143 次已应用 SD-LoRA loss', '7B record: 149 round Scores + 143 applied SD-LoRA losses')}</li><li>{t('1.7B 记录：160 轮 Score + 44 个候选位置 + 7 个可核验 loss', '1.7B record: 160 round Scores + 44 candidate locations + 7 authoritative losses')}</li><li>{t('3B 记录：123 轮 Score + 31 次候选训练 loss', '3B record: 123 round Scores + 31 candidate-training losses')}</li></ul></article>
        <article><span>02 · FROZEN FINAL</span><h3>{t('为什么 W&B 没有每个 checkpoint 的“最终 128 题分数”', 'Why W&B does not contain a frozen-128 score for every checkpoint')}</h3><p>{t('那 128 题被锁到训练结束才打开。如果训练中每隔几轮就跑一次，它就会从 final panel 变成 validation / 调参集。7B 的 49.33 和 1.7B 的 37.60 都是在最终状态固定以后才测。', 'The 128 tasks stayed locked until training ended. Re-running them every few rounds would turn the final panel into a validation/tuning set. The 7B 49.33 and 1.7B 37.60 were measured only after the final state was frozen.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>03 · POST-HOC</span><h3>{t('历史 checkpoint 仍然可以事后重放，但必须换一个名字', 'Historical checkpoints can still be replayed later, but it is a different measurement')}</h3><p>{t('7B 的完整 lineage、Memory / Skill / Agent 状态和 SD-LoRA component store 都已归档，所以可以在训练结束后挑 8–12 个里程碑重建并统一回放。这样的曲线只能标成 post-hoc checkpoint replay，不能说它当时参与了 checkpoint selection。', 'The full 7B lineage, Memory / Skill / Agent state, and SD-LoRA component store are archived, so 8–12 milestone states can be reconstructed and replayed after training. That curve must be labeled post-hoc checkpoint replay; it was not used for checkpoint selection during training.')}</p></article>
